---
description: General development principles
alwaysApply: true
---

- Understand the existing code before making changes.
- Prefer existing patterns and utilities over introducing new ones.
- Make the smallest clean change that solves the problem.
- Do not modify unrelated code.
- Avoid premature abstraction and overengineering.
- Keep code simple, readable and maintainable.
- Preserve existing behavior unless explicitly asked to change it.
- Consider edge cases and error handling.
- Remove unused code introduced during the task.
- Verify changes with appropriate tests, type checks or builds.
